  "$comment": "Protocol 1.5. Data-channel messages both libraries must accept or refuse with parse_screen_dc_message / parseScreenDcMessage (rules.screen_content, rules.screen_cursor); every refusal is MALFORMED_MESSAGE. `direction` is the receiving side's vocabulary, `text` the exact message string (padding is spaces before the closing brace). Written byte for byte by shared/python/scripts/make_fixtures.py and shared/ts/scripts/make-fixtures.ts; the PNGs are test images built there (1x1 RGBA, the large one padded with a tEXt chunk).",
